# Data visualisation

Apply the brand guidance’s clarity, accessibility and accuracy principles to real household questions. Operational charts follow [Charts and tables](../components/charts.html), [Chart colour](chart-colour.html) and the production Energy adapter. Project publicity graphics are a separate output. The same accuracy and accessibility principles apply, but a promotional layout must not replace an operational chart.

## Choose the right data pattern

| What someone needs to understand | Design guidance and examples |
| --- | --- |
| Change over time or a comparison | [Charts and tables](../components/charts.html) and [working chart examples](../components/chart-examples.html) |
| Several related indicators checked repeatedly | [Dashboard monitoring and household overviews](../patterns/home.html) |
| Location, distance or a spatial pattern | [OpenStreetMap-based maps and location records](../home-assistant/maps-and-zones.html) |
| Categories, increasing values or change from a target | [Chart and map colour scales](chart-colour.html) |
| Flow, part-to-whole or a bounded reading | [Energy flow and other chart families](../home-assistant/energy-flow-and-other-charts.html) |

These are design-system specifications and working reference examples. They do not update a Home Assistant installation. The source site calls this **Brand data**; here it is ordinary data-design guidance, independent of a household’s name or logo.

